        "original_id": "48d4a486-4a28-5e05-951f-c41932fb86eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sacramento Deep Water Ship Channel, Contra Costa Canal, Port of Sacramento, Sacramento River, San Francisco Bay, West Sacramento, California\n- Organizations: United States Army Corps of Engineers\n- Topics: canals, aqueducts, construction timelines\n\nFacts:\n- Construction of the Contra Costa Canal began in 1937 in California.\n- The Contra Costa Canal was completed in 1948 after delays caused by World War II shortages in labor and materials.\n- The Sacramento Deep Water Ship Channel was completed in 1963 by the United States Army Corps of Engineers.\n- The Sacramento Deep Water Ship Channel, also known as the Sacramento River Deep Water Ship Channel or SRDWSC, is a canal from the Port of Sacramento in West Sacramento, California, to the Sacramento River, which flows into San Francisco Bay.\n- The Contra Costa Canal is a 47-mile aqueduct in California.",
